arm64: dts: mediatek: gemini: disable the watchdog's external reset (B-30)

The RGU's external-reset output reaches the PMIC on this board, and the PMIC
powers the machine off instead of restarting it. Since mtk_wdt_restart() is the
platform's system restart handler, that made every `reboot` look like the device
had died. Clearing EXRST_EN makes the reset internal and immediate.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts
@@ -2037,3 +2037,16 @@
 &scpsys {
 	mfg-supply = <&vgpu>;
 };
+
+/*
+ * GEMINI (B-30): the RGU's external-reset output reaches the PMIC, which powers
+ * the board OFF instead of restarting it. Since mtk_wdt_restart() is this
+ * platform's system restart handler, that made every `reboot` look like the
+ * device had died — no USB, no network, dark panel, not even an LK splash — and
+ * only the power button brought it back. Measured 2026-08-20: with EXRST_EN
+ * cleared the same WDT_SWRST restarts the SoC and the system is back on the
+ * network in 77 s.
+ */
+&watchdog {
+	mediatek,disable-extrst;
+};
